<%# One person that the draft names, and what they are called at each network.

    ⚠️ **All four fields must render for every row, in the same order.** The names are
    `mentions[][token]` and one for each network key, and Rails starts a new hash when a key
    repeats. A row that omits one field would move each field below it by one. It is the rule of
    `posts[][text]`. The loop below reads the same list for every row, thus the order cannot drift.

    ⚠️ **A field takes a handle OR plain words.** A person with no account at a network still has a
    name, and the post must be able to say it. The action reads the shape and decides. An empty
    field posts the token with no "@". Thus no value here can ever tag the wrong account.
%>
<div class="social-mention" data-social-target="mention">
  <%# ⚠️ The token is not editable here: the words of the post are where the owner writes it. The
      hidden field is what puts it in the form. %>
  <input type="hidden" name="mentions[][token]" value="<%= mention.token %>" data-mention-token>

  <p class="social-mention__token" data-mention-label><%= mention.token %></p>

  <% networks.each do |network| %>
    <wa-input name="mentions[][<%= network.key %>]" label="<%= network.name %>"
              value="<%= mention.value(network.key) %>"
              placeholder="<%= placeholders[network.key] %>"
              autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
              data-mention-network="<%= network.key %>">
    </wa-input>
  <% end %>
</div>
